---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import missingPage from '../assets/missing-page.svg';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`404: Page Not Found | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="The page is missing, but here is a very short history of HTTP 404 before you head back."
		/>
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main aria-labelledby="page-title" aria-describedby="error-code">
			<article>
				<div class="title">
					<p class="error-code" id="error-code">404 - Page not found</p>
					<h1 id="page-title">A Brief History of Not Finding Things</h1>
					<hr />
				</div>
				<nav class="actions" aria-label="Page recovery">
					<a class="home-link" href="/">Back to home</a>
					<a href="/blog/">Browse the blog</a>
				</nav>
				<figure class="search-party">
					<Image
						src={missingPage}
						alt="A puzzled robot uses a magnifying glass to inspect an empty box labelled PAGE."
						loading="eager"
					/>
					<figcaption>The search team has found a box. Progress.</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<p>
					By May 1996, the <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1945.html#section-9.4"
						>HTTP/1.0 specification</a
					> already documented <strong>404 Not Found</strong>: the server couldn't find anything
					matching the requested address. The web has been losing things professionally for decades.
				</p>
				<p>
					The first 4 puts it in HTTP's "client error" family; the remaining digits identify the
					particular status. That sounds accusatory, but it isn't a performance review. Links age,
					pages move, and websites occasionally rearrange the furniture without telling anyone.
				</p>
				<p>
					Today's <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.5.5"
						>HTTP standard</a
					> still won't say whether a 404 is temporary or permanent. There is a separate{' '}
					<strong>410 Gone</strong> for something likely to stay gone: the protocol equivalent of
					"it's not you, it's the URL." This one is a 404. No page, no firm conclusions, and apparently
					enough spare time for a history lesson.
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		min-height: 100vh;
		min-height: 100svh;
	}

	main {
		box-sizing: border-box;
		flex: 1;
		width: 760px;
		max-width: 100%;
		padding-block: 3em;
	}

	.title {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		padding: 1em 0;
		text-align: center;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.error-code {
		display: inline-block;
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 4px;
		background: #f1f3ff;
		color: var(--accent-dark);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.4;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5em;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.4em);
	}

	article > p {
		margin: 0 0 1.5em;
	}

	.search-party {
		max-width: 440px;
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.search-party img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	article a {
		text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
	}

	article a:hover {
		color: var(--accent-dark);
	}

	article a:focus-visible {
		outline: 3px solid var(--accent-dark);
		outline-offset: 4px;
	}

	.actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.actions a {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		min-height: 44px;
		padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--accent);
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.actions a:hover {
		background: rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}

	.actions .home-link {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
	}

	.actions .home-link:hover {
		border-color: var(--accent-dark);
		background: var(--accent-dark);
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		main {
			padding-block: 2em;
		}
	}
</style>
